# Navigation & wayfinding improvements

**Severity:** Medium
**Area:** `templates/base.html` (nav), lesson activity templates, vocab/grammar detail templates

## Problems

### 1. No active state on nav links

The top navigation (`Lezione`, `Vocabolario`, `Grammatica`, `Profilo`) shows all four links with identical styling regardless of which page you're on. There's no visual indicator for the current section.

### 2. No back navigation between lesson activities

Once a student advances past a grammar explanation, there's no way to go back and re-read it. This is especially painful when a drill references content from the grammar card ("All of these appeared in the grammar section above") but the student can't return to it.

### 3. No breadcrumbs on detail pages

The vocab word page (`/vocab/word/{entry_id}`) and grammar detail page (`/grammar/{code}`) have no "Back to list" link. The only way to return is the browser back button or the top nav. (`grammar-chunk.html` has a `javascript:history.back()` link, but the other two detail pages don't.)

### 4. No lesson history accessible from nav

Past lessons are only visible buried in the profile page. A student who wants to revisit a completed lesson's content has to go Profile -> scroll to "Lezioni recenti" -> click.

---

## Implementation plan

> **Scope boundary with ticket #2:** This ticket is purely about navigation chrome, links, and route behaviour. It does NOT touch text encoding, HTML escaping, `|safe` filters, markdown rendering, or `<span lang>` stripping — all of those belong to ticket #2.

### 1. Nav active state

**No route changes needed.** Jinja2's `request` object is already available in all templates (FastAPI injects it). Use `request.url.path` in `base.html` to highlight the current section.

#### `templates/base.html` (lines 20-30)

Replace the four static `<a>` tags with path-based active class:

```html
<nav>
  <div class="site-container">
    <a href="/lezione/" {% if request.url.path.startswith('/lezione') %}class="active"{% endif %}>{{ t("nav_lesson") }}</a>
    <a href="/vocab" {% if request.url.path.startswith('/vocab') %}class="active"{% endif %}>{{ t("nav_vocab") }}</a>
    <a href="/grammar" {% if request.url.path.startswith('/grammar') %}class="active"{% endif %}>{{ t("nav_grammar") }}</a>
    <a href="/profilo" {% if request.url.path.startswith('/profilo') %}class="active"{% endif %}>{{ t("nav_profile") }}</a>
    ...
  </div>
</nav>
```

#### `static/style.css` (after line 75)

Add one rule:

```css
nav a.active { color: var(--c-charcoal); font-weight: 600; }
```

Optionally add a bottom border (`border-bottom: 2px solid var(--c-terracotta)`) for stronger visual weight. Keep it simple — no JS needed.

---

### 2. Back navigation in lesson activities

The existing GET handler `lezione_activity` (`routes/lezione.py:187`) already renders any activity by index — it does **not** enforce `idx == lesson.current_index`. So navigating to a past activity URL already works. The missing pieces are: (a) UI to get there, and (b) preventing re-submission of completed activities.

#### Approach: clickable progress bar + read-only past activities

**a) `lezione-progress.html`** — make completed segments clickable

Currently renders a plain fill bar. Replace with a segmented bar where each completed activity is a clickable link:

```html
{# Expects: lesson, idx, total #}
<div class="lesson-progress">
  <div class="progress-segments">
    {% for a in lesson.activities %}
    {% set seg_class %}{% if loop.index0 < idx %}completed{% elif loop.index0 == idx %}current{% else %}upcoming{% endif %}{% endset %}
    {% if loop.index0 < idx %}
    <a href="/lezione/{{ lesson.id }}/activity/{{ loop.index0 }}"
       class="progress-seg {{ seg_class }}" title="{{ a.title }}"></a>
    {% else %}
    <div class="progress-seg {{ seg_class }}" title="{{ a.title }}"></div>
    {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <div class="progress-label">{{ t("progress_label", current=idx + 1, total=total) }}</div>
</div>
```

Add CSS for segments:

```css
.progress-segments { display: flex; gap: 3px; height: 6px; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
.progress-seg { flex: 1; border-radius: 3px; background: var(--c-border); }
.progress-seg.completed { background: var(--c-olive); cursor: pointer; }
.progress-seg.completed:hover { opacity: 0.8; }
.progress-seg.current { background: var(--c-terracotta); }
a.progress-seg { display: block; text-decoration: none; }
```

**b) Route: pass `is_review` flag** — `routes/lezione.py:187` `lezione_activity()`

After loading the activity, add to context:

```python
is_review = (
    activity.status in (ActivityStatus.COMPLETED, ActivityStatus.SKIPPED)
    and idx < lesson.current_index
)
ctx["is_review"] = is_review
```

No new route needed. The existing GET handler works as-is.

**c) Activity templates: hide forms when `is_review`**

In each template that has a submit form (`lezione-activity-grammar.html`, `lezione-activity-drill.html`, `lezione-activity-reading.html`, `lezione-activity-writing.html`), wrap the form/submit section:

```html
{% if is_review %}
<div class="review-banner">
  <a href="/lezione/{{ lesson.id }}/activity/{{ lesson.current_index }}" class="continue-btn">
    {{ t("back_to_current") }}
  </a>
</div>
{% else %}
  {# existing form/buttons #}
{% endif %}
```

For **drill** review: also show the student's previous answers from `activity.result` if available.

For **grammar** review: the "Ho capito / Skip" buttons are replaced with just the "Back to current" link. The content is already visible (it's `activity.content`).

For **vocab_review**: this one is trickier (SRS card flip). Simplest: don't make vocab segments clickable in the progress bar (they're transient). Or skip is_review for vocab type.

**d) Add i18n key:**

```json
"back_to_current": "Back to current activity"
```

#### Files changed

| File | Change |
|------|--------|
| `templates/lezione-progress.html` | Segmented clickable bar |
| `templates/lezione-activity-grammar.html` | Hide buttons when `is_review` |
| `templates/lezione-activity-drill.html` | Hide form when `is_review`, show past answers |
| `templates/lezione-activity-reading.html` | Hide form when `is_review` |
| `templates/lezione-activity-writing.html` | Hide form when `is_review` |
| `routes/lezione.py` | Add `is_review` to context dict (line ~203) |
| `static/style.css` | Progress segment styles, review banner |
| `i18n/*.json` | `back_to_current` key |

