### 4. Lesson history from nav

Currently `GET /lezione/` (`routes/lezione.py:57`) redirects to the active lesson or `/lezione/new`. When there's no active lesson, show a landing page with lesson history + a "Start new lesson" button instead of immediately redirecting.

#### `routes/lezione.py` — modify `lezione_index()` (line 57)

```python
@router.get("/lezione/", response_class=HTMLResponse)
async def lezione_index(request: Request, student: Student = Depends(get_current_student)):
    active = await Lesson.find_one({"student_id": student.id, "status": LessonStatus.ACTIVE})
    if active:
        if active.generating and active.current_index >= len(active.activities):
            return RedirectResponse(url=f"/lezione/{active.id}/generating")
        return RedirectResponse(url=activity_url(active.id, active.current_index))

    # No active lesson — show history + start button
    recent_lessons = await Lesson.find(
        {"student_id": student.id, "status": LessonStatus.COMPLETED}
    ).sort(-Lesson.completed_at).limit(20).to_list()

    scenario_slugs = {l.scenario_slug for l in recent_lessons if l.scenario_slug}
    scenarios_list = await CurriculumScenario.find(
        {"slug": {"$in": list(scenario_slugs)}}
    ).to_list() if scenario_slugs else []
    scenario_labels = {s.slug: s.label for s in scenarios_list}

    lesson_history = [
        {"lesson": l, "scenario_label": scenario_labels.get(l.scenario_slug, "")}
        for l in recent_lessons
    ]

    profile = await get_profile(student.id)
    cefr = profile.cefr_estimate if profile else "A0"

    return templates.TemplateResponse(
        request=request,
        name="lezione-index.html",
        context={"lesson_history": lesson_history, "cefr": cefr},
    )
```

Add `CurriculumScenario` to the imports at the top of the file.

#### New template: `templates/lezione-index.html`

```html
{% extends "base.html" %}
{% block title %}{{ t("nav_lesson") }} — Maestro{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<div class="lesson-index">
  <div class="lesson-index-header">
    <h1>{{ t("nav_lesson") }}</h1>
    <a class="btn-primary" href="/lezione/new">{{ t("lesson_new_btn") }}</a>
  </div>

  {% if lesson_history %}
  <h2>{{ t("profile_recent_lessons") }}</h2>
  <div class="history-list">
    {% for item in lesson_history %}
    <a href="/lezione/{{ item.lesson.id }}/complete" class="history-row">
      <span class="history-date">{{ item.lesson.completed_at.strftime('%d/%m') if item.lesson.completed_at else '' }}</span>
      <span class="history-topic">{{ item.lesson.topic_title or '-' }}</span>
      <span class="history-scenario">{{ item.scenario_label }}</span>
    </a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% else %}
  <p class="empty-hint">{{ t("lesson_no_history") }}</p>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endblock %}
```

#### i18n key

```json
"lesson_no_history": "No lessons yet. Start your first one!"
```

#### Files changed

| File | Change |
|------|--------|
| `routes/lezione.py` | Modify `lezione_index()`, add `CurriculumScenario` import |
| `templates/lezione-index.html` | **New file** — lesson landing with history |
| `static/style.css` | `.lesson-index-header` flex layout |
| `i18n/*.json` | `lesson_no_history` key |

---

## Suggested implementation order

1. **Nav active state** (smallest, standalone, immediate visual improvement)
2. **Breadcrumbs on detail pages** (tiny, standalone)
3. **Lesson history from nav** (moderate, one new template + route change)
4. **Back navigation in lessons** (largest, touches multiple templates + route context)

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Current nav section is visually highlighted
- [ ] Student can navigate backward within a lesson to revisit earlier activities (read-only)
- [ ] Detail pages (vocab word, grammar point) have a back link to their parent list
- [ ] Past lessons are accessible without going through the profile page
